            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for profit, then the Gujarati for loss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: હિસાબ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હિસાબ — hisāb — \"reckoning, accounts\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દુકાનદાર સાંજે હિસાબ કરે છે. — dukāndār sā̃je hisāb kare che — \"The shopkeeper does the accounts in the evening.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હિસાબ (hisāb) is a loan from Arabic ḥisāb, \"counting, reckoning\", which reached Gujarati through Persian. Its Arabic root is ḥ-s-b, \"to count\" (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
